    descriptionEn: "Brazilian metal emerged in the mid-1980s, mainly in Belo Horizonte and São Paulo, where bands took up heavy metal and thrash. Sepultura, formed in Belo Horizonte in 1984, became the standard-bearer of the genre with Beneath the Remains (1989) and Arise (1991), before bringing Brazilian percussion into Roots (1996). Angra, from São Paulo, established a melodic power metal marked by classical and Brazilian influences from Angels Cry (1993), while Krisiun, from Rio Grande do Sul, represents brutal death metal. Sepultura influenced generations of bands around the world.",
