    descriptionEn: "Brazilian punk rock was born in the late 1970s and early 1980s in the working-class suburbs of São Paulo and in the capital, Brasília, as the military dictatorship was coming to an end. In Brasília, Aborto Elétrico turned into Legião Urbana, while São Paulo saw the rise of Cólera, formed in 1979, Inocentes and Ratos de Porão, created in 1981. The compilation 'Grito Suburbano' (1982), gathering several bands from the São Paulo outskirts, became the scene's founding document. The sound is fast and unadorned, with overdriven guitars, Portuguese vocals and lyrics about urban violence, poverty and repression. Ratos de Porão later moved toward hardcore and crossover thrash, influencing Brazilian extreme metal.",
