    descriptionFr: "Le brostep émerge vers 2010-2011, principalement aux États-Unis et au Royaume-Uni, comme une évolution agressive du dubstep traditionnel. Cette mutation sonore trouve ses racines dans le dubstep londonien des années 2000, mais s'en écarte radicalement en privilégiant l'intensité brute sur la subtilité atmosphérique. Les wobbles, générés par des oscillateurs low-pass filtrés, deviennent la signature du genre. Culturellement, le brostep divise la communauté dubstep puriste mais conquiert les festivals mainstream américains, symbolisant la commercialisation controversée d'un genre initialement underground londonien.",
    descriptionEn: "Brostep emerged around 2010-2011, primarily in the United States and United Kingdom, as an aggressive evolution of traditional dubstep.\n\nThe genre fused UK dubstep's foundational elements with American electronic dance music sensibilities, incorporating influences from metal, hardcore punk, and electro house. Pioneer artists drew from Skrillex's signature sound design and Rusko's earlier wobble basslines.\n\nHeavy sidechaining compressors and multiband distortion processors create the characteristic aggressive textures.\n\nProductions employ extreme compression ratios (8:1 or higher), high-frequency emphasis, and dramatic dynamic contrasts between sparse breakdowns and explosive choruses.\n\nCulturally, brostep became synonymous with American festival culture, particularly Electric Daisy Carnival and Ultra Music Festival, attracting mainstream audiences while simultaneously creating division within underground dubstep communities who favored the genre's darker, more minimal UK origins.",
