    descriptionFr: "Le djent émerge au milieu des années 2000, principalement en Suède avec Meshuggah comme précurseur, avant de se mondialiser via internet. Ce genre hybride puise dans le metal progressif, le math rock et les polyrythmes jazz-fusion, cristallisant une esthétique sonore ultra-moderne. Culturellement, ce genre incarne l'ère numérique du metal : production home-studio, diffusion virale, communautés en ligne. Il symbolise une génération de musiciens techniciens, repoussant les limites de la complexité rythmique tout en conservant une accessibilité mélodique, influençant profondément le metal contemporain.",
    descriptionEn: "Djent emerged in the mid-2000s, primarily in Sweden with Meshuggah as pioneers, before globalizing through internet communities. This hybrid genre draws from progressive metal, math rock, and jazz-fusion polyrhythms, crystallizing an ultra-modern sonic aesthetic. The genre's harmonic language blends dissonant intervals with ambient textures, often incorporating clean passages that contrast with aggressive polyrhythmic sections. Culturally, djent embodies metal's digital era: home-studio production, viral distribution, online communities. It represents a generation of technical musicians pushing rhythmic complexity boundaries while maintaining melodic accessibility. This movement has profoundly influenced contemporary metal, spawning countless bedroom producers and redefining heavy music's relationship with technology and global connectivity.",
