    descriptionEn: "Emo was born in the mid-1980s in Washington, D.C., in the wake of hardcore punk, with bands such as Rites of Spring, whose lyrics were more personal and intense. In the 1990s the scene spread across the United States: Sunny Day Real Estate released 'Diary' in 1994, and American Football put out its only album of the era in 1999, a landmark of 'midwest emo'. The sound blends arpeggiated or distorted guitars, vocals that move from whispers to screams, and very intimate lyrics. In the 2000s, My Chemical Romance and others brought it to the mainstream, before the revivals of the 2010s.",
