    descriptionEn: "Euskal musika (Basque music) emerges from the Pyrenean territories of the Basque Country, flourishing since medieval times across the French-Spanish border. 'Euskal' derives from 'euskera,' the ancestral Basque language, among Europe's oldest surviving tongues. This millennial musical tradition blends Celtic, Iberian, and Gascon influences, forging a unique sonic heritage. Tempos range from contemplative andante in sacred chants to vivacious allegro in festive mutxikos. Euskal musika transcends mere folklore: serving as cultural cement, it accompanies communal rituals from weddings to patron saint celebrations. In frontons and public squares, it perpetuates social cohesion among this transborder people, resisting cultural assimilation through centuries-old oral transmission and contemporary innovations that honor ancestral heritage. This living tradition continues evolving while preserving its distinctive modal harmonies and intricate polyrhythmic structures.",
