    name: "goregrind",
    descriptionFr: "Le goregrind émerge au milieu des années 1980, principalement en Angleterre avec Carcass et aux États-Unis avec Repulsion. Ce sous-genre hybride du grindcore emprunte son nom à la fusion entre 'gore' (sang/violence graphique) et 'grind' (broyer), reflétant son esthétique viscérale inspirée des films d'horreur série B. Le chant alterne entre growls gutturaux inintelligibles et 'pig squeals' aigus, créant une dichotomie sonore saisissante. Culturellement, le goregrind interroge la fascination morbide contemporaine tout en défiant les conventions musicales traditionnelles, influençant des générations de musiciens extrêmes et redéfinissant les limites de l'expression artistique underground.",
    descriptionEn: "Goregrind emerged in the mid-1980s, primarily in England with Carcass and in the United States with Repulsion. This hybrid subgenre of grindcore derives its name from the fusion of 'gore' (graphic blood/violence) and 'grind' (to crush), reflecting its visceral aesthetic inspired by B-horror films. Vocals alternate between unintelligible guttural growls and high-pitched 'pig squeals,' creating a striking sonic dichotomy. The production often features pitch-shifted vocals and samples from horror films or medical documentaries. Culturally, goregrind interrogates contemporary morbid fascination while challenging traditional musical conventions, influencing generations of extreme musicians and redefining the boundaries of underground artistic expression within metal's most radical fringes.",
