    name: "harmonica blues",
    descriptionFr: "L'harmonica blues naît dans le Delta du Mississippi vers 1920-1930, fusionnant les traditions africaines du mbira avec l'instrument européen importé par les colons allemands. Ce genre émerge des work songs et field hollers des plantations, transformé par des musiciens comme Little Walter et Sonny Boy Williamson qui révolutionnent l'instrument. Culturellement, l'harmonica blues transcende les barrières raciales, devenant l'expression universelle de la condition ouvrière. Son impact social est immense : instrument accessible financièrement, il démocratise la création musicale et influence rock, folk et country, de Bob Dylan aux Rolling Stones.",
    descriptionEn: "Harmonica blues emerged in the Mississippi Delta around 1920-1930, fusing African mbira traditions with the European harmonica brought by German settlers. This genre evolved from plantation work songs and field hollers, revolutionized by pioneers like Little Walter and Sonny Boy Williamson who transformed the instrument's possibilities. The genre's cultural significance transcends racial boundaries, becoming the universal expression of working-class struggles. Its social impact was profound: as an affordable instrument, it democratized musical creation and profoundly influenced rock, folk, and country music, inspiring artists from Bob Dylan to the Rolling Stones, establishing the harmonica as an essential voice in American music.",
