    descriptionFr: "L'indie córdoba émerge au début des années 2000 dans la ville étudiante de Córdoba, Argentine, fruit d'une synthèse unique entre l'indie rock anglo-saxon et les sonorités rioplatenses. Culturellement, l'indie córdoba reflète la mélancolie urbaine de la génération post-crise économique argentine, exprimant à travers ses textes en spanglish les préoccupations d'une jeunesse cosmopolite tiraillée entre traditions locales et influences globalisées. Ce genre a profondément marqué la scène musicale sud-américaine indépendante.",
    descriptionEn: "Indie córdoba emerged in early 2000s Córdoba, Argentina, blending Anglo-Saxon indie rock with distinctive Rioplatense soundscapes. Named after the provincial capital, this movement originated in underground venues throughout the Güemes district's student quarter. Lyrically delivered in fluid Spanglish, tracks explore post-economic crisis urban melancholy, capturing a cosmopolitan generation caught between local traditions and global influences. The sound typically layers jagged guitar arpeggios over analog basslines, while vintage Chamberlin string sections add nostalgic textures. Culturally, indie córdoba represents Argentina's independent music renaissance, influencing subsequent South American alternative movements. Its introspective aesthetic and bilingual approach have resonated internationally, establishing Córdoba as an unexpected epicenter of Latin American indie innovation.",
