    descriptionFr: "L'Irish Black Metal émerge au début des années 1990 en Irlande du Nord, fusion révolutionnaire entre la férocité du black metal scandinave et les mélodies celtiques ancestrales.\n\nLes progressions exploitent les modes doriens et mixolydiens, créant une mélancolie distincte renforcée par des ambiances de reverb cathédralesque.\n\nCulturellement, ce mouvement exprime l'identité irlandaise post-Troubles, transformant la douleur historique en catharsis artistique. Il participe au renouveau de la fierté culturelle celtique tout en embrassant l'esthétique transgressive du black metal, créant un pont entre tradition ancestrale et modernité extrême.",
    descriptionEn: "Irish Black Metal emerged in early 1990s Northern Ireland as a revolutionary fusion between Scandinavian black metal ferocity and ancestral Celtic melodies.\n\nOriginating primarily in Belfast and Dublin circa 1993-1995, the movement fused second-wave Scandinavian black metal with traditional Irish folk music, incorporating bodhrán percussion, uilleann pipes, and fiddle arrangements.\n\nProduction maintained the characteristic lo-fi aesthetic using analog four-track recording, creating atmospheric soundscapes that evoked Ireland's mystical landscapes.\n\nCulturally, Irish black metal emerged during post-Troubles reconciliation, channeling nationalist sentiment and pre-Christian mythology into extreme metal expression. The genre celebrated Celtic paganism, ancient Irish folklore, and resistance themes, distinguishing itself from Norwegian counterparts through its focus on Irish historical narratives rather than Satanic imagery. This created a unique subset that influenced atmospheric black metal globally while preserving Ireland's musical heritage within extreme metal contexts.",
