    name: "liquid funk",
    descriptionFr: "Le liquid funk émerge au milieu des années 1990 à Londres, particulièrement dans les clubs d'Hoxton et Shoreditch, avant de se propager internationalement. Né de la fusion entre le jazz fusion, la soul et les breakbeats accélérés, le liquid funk puise dans l'héritage du jazz-funk des années 1970 et des productions hip-hop de Detroit. Culturellement, le liquid funk transcende les barrières sociales du drum and bass underground, séduisant un public plus large grâce à sa dimension contemplative. Il influence durablement la musique électronique contemporaine, inspirant l'émergence du future garage et du neo-soul électronique.",
    descriptionEn: "Liquid funk emerged in mid-1990s London, particularly in Hoxton and Shoreditch clubs, before spreading internationally. The term 'liquid' refers to the melodic fluidity characterizing this drum and bass subgenre, contrasting with the harsher 'hardstep' sounds. Born from jazz fusion, soul, and accelerated breakbeats, liquid funk draws from 1970s jazz-funk heritage and Detroit hip-hop productions. The production aesthetic emphasizes warm analog compression and subtle reverb processing, creating immersive soundscapes. Culturally, liquid funk transcended underground drum and bass barriers, attracting broader audiences through its contemplative dimension. It profoundly influenced contemporary electronic music, inspiring future garage and electronic neo-soul emergence. The genre fostered a more inclusive rave culture, moving beyond the masculine hardcore scene to embrace diverse demographics seeking sophisticated dancefloor experiences with emotional depth.",
