    descriptionEn: "Metal guitar originated in Birmingham, England, between 1968-1970, crystallized by Black Sabbath's revolutionary use of the diabolical tritone.\n\nEvolving from blues rock, hard rock, and classical music traditions, metal guitar fused Hendrix's distortion innovations with classical harmonic complexity and Celtic/folk modal scales. The genre emerged from working-class industrial cities, reflecting post-war disillusionment and countercultural rebellion.\n\nDown-tuned guitars (often Drop D or lower) create darker tonalities, while high-gain distortion produces the signature saturated sound.\n\nProduction emphasizes palm-muted rhythms, tremolo picking, and layered guitar harmonies creating walls of sound.",
