    descriptionEn: "Progressive house appeared in the early 1990s in the United Kingdom, in the wake of house and techno, with clubs such as Renaissance in Mansfield. It is marked by long, slowly building tracks: round basslines, synth pads, repeated melodic motifs and blended transitions, designed for long mixes. Sasha and John Digweed are its leading figures, notably through the mix “Northern Exposure” (1996). In the 2000s, Canada's Deadmau5 and Sweden's Eric Prydz brought it a festival audience, with tracks such as “Strobe” (2009) and “Opus” (2016). The genre fed into melodic trance and much of electro house.",
