    descriptionEn: "Reggae cover means reworking pop, soul or rock songs in a reggae style. The practice is old in Jamaica: as early as the 1960s, Kingston producers adapted American soul hits into ska and rocksteady. In the United Kingdom, UB40, from Birmingham, made it their specialty with Labour of Love (1983), which includes Red Red Wine, a Neil Diamond song that became a British number one. In the 1990s, Big Mountain with Baby, I Love Your Way (1994) and Pato Banton with Baby Come Back (1994) carried on the tradition. These covers introduced reggae to a worldwide pop audience.",
