    name: "rock drums",
    descriptionFr: "Le rock drums émerge au milieu des années 1960 en Angleterre et aux États-Unis, révolutionnant l'art percussif occidental.\n\nFusionnant les traditions du jazz, du blues et du rhythm & blues, ce style transforme radicalement l'approche percussive.\n\nLes breaks dynamiques, les fills complexes et la technique du « back beat » deviennent signatures. Les progressions s'articulent autour de motifs répétitifs hypnotiques, amplifiés par la stéréophonie naissante.\n\nCulturellement, ce style accompagne la révolution sociale des années 1960-70, symbolisant la rébellion générationnelle. Il influence profondément la production musicale moderne, établissant la batterie comme instrument soliste à part entière et redéfinissant l'esthétique sonore contemporaine dans le rock progressif, hard rock et metal.",
    descriptionEn: "Rock drums crystallized in mid-1960s Britain and America, fundamentally transforming Western percussive artistry.\n\nEmerging from blues shuffles and country backbeats, rock drumming fused African-American rhythmic traditions with British beat sensibilities, particularly in Liverpool and London's vibrant music scenes. Early pioneers incorporated jazz techniques with amplified folk and R&B patterns.\n\nHi-hats, crash cymbals, and eventually double bass pedals defined the setup.\n\nFill patterns became increasingly complex, incorporating syncopation and cross-stick techniques. Studio innovations included close-miking, reverb chambers, and compression, creating the punchy, present sound that defined rock's sonic signature.\n\nRock drumming became synonymous with youth rebellion and cultural revolution, providing the rhythmic backbone for social movements throughout the 1960s-70s, establishing percussion as a lead instrument rather than mere timekeeping accompaniment.",
