    descriptionEn: "Terrorcore emerged in the early 1990s from the Dutch and German hardcore techno scenes, particularly in Rotterdam and Berlin's underground rave circuits.\n\nEvolving from gabber, speedcore, and industrial music traditions, terrorcore incorporated elements from death metal and horror film soundtracks.\n\nProduction emphasizes maximum loudness through aggressive limiting and multiband compression.\n\nCulturally, terrorcore represented a rejection of commercial dance music, appealing to hardcore techno purists seeking increasingly extreme experiences. Its confrontational aesthetic influenced speedcore and breakcore subgenres, while its DIY distribution through underground labels and early internet communities established templates for extreme electronic music circulation. The genre's uncompromising intensity reflected 1990s rave culture's darker undercurrents.",
